    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe `initials` field is served on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response, which maps the `Owner` entity to `OwnerDto` via MapStruct. I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` (read-only string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the code-generated `OwnerDto` gains an `initials` field/getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression that computes initials as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\",\n       expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nFor `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` this produces `\"J.S.\"`, matching the test. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
